Skill edit_ai_task {
  label: 'Change a scheduled AI task'
  description: "Use when the user changes the task drafted in this chat (a follow-up such as “make it 9 AM”, or an “… instead” button), or explicitly asks to update, edit or change another task by name: its schedule, source, rule, rows, acceptance criteria or attachment. Typical phrasings: “update my revenue alert to 9 AM”, “edit the Monday digest's threshold”, “Run at 8:00 AM instead”, “Use Ecommerce Official instead”, “Alert at 30% instead”, “Attach a chart instead”, “Change the acceptance criteria”, “show the top 10 instead”. Do not use for a request for a new task, schedule, report or alert, even on a subject an existing task covers (use create_ai_task), or for previewing a task's result (use run_ai_task). Load write_ai_task_brief in the same step as this skill: it saves the change."
  invocation: 'auto'
  disabled: H.git.is_production
  content: @md
    # Change a scheduled AI task

    Change a task only when it's this chat's draft or the user explicitly asks to update, edit or change it by name. Any other request is a new task: use `create_ai_task`. Read the task file, and its schedule entry only for a time change. Open an earlier chat only when the user points to it. Change only what they asked for, preserve every other line, and show the diff.

    ## Apply the change

    - **An "… instead" button is the whole change:** apply it without a card. Time updates the Schedule line and schedule entry in UTC; source updates the Source line and every named field after `create_ai_task`'s source checks; "Attach … instead" updates the Attachment line and attach step, never a criterion, as `add_ai_task_delivery` writes them.
    - **"Change the acceptance criteria" on its own:** ask "How should the acceptance criteria change?" with 2–3 likely edits, each quoting its criterion.
    - **A typed change is the whole change:** update every use in Definitions, message step and checking criterion.
    - **A new vague word** ("a lot") uses `create_ai_task`'s Metric, Ranking or Threshold card; recipients or a send condition use `add_ai_task_delivery`. Load the owner skill before its rules or cards.
    - **An older task** whose brief still loads `format_ai_task_output`, starts with Step 0, pastes a Delivery rules block or sets the message's layout ("every <group>", values per line) gets its Steps and criteria rewritten in the current form, keeping what they cover.
    - **A Schedule line naming another timezone** becomes UTC with any change, cron kept.

    Save as `write_ai_task_brief` says, then reply with the update report below, not the draft report.

    ## Show the update report

    The reply's only text: the draft line under the heading, then only what changed, then the changed files.
    - **Bold**, in this report only: the words this change added, in rows and criteria. Kept words stay plain even if saved bold (✓ "Sends one message to #sales and **one email to you@x.com**" when only the email is new).
    - **Rows:** `~~<old>~~ → <new>`, with the draft report's icons and labels ("📨 Delivery", never 📧) and `add_ai_task_delivery`'s values ("~~None~~ → **Viz · PNG**", "~~Slack · #sales~~ → Slack · #sales; **Email · you@x.com**"). Leave the table out when no row changed.
    - **Criteria:** "▢ " paragraphs under Acceptance criteria, never in the table.
      - Changed: `▢ ~~<old>~~ → <new>`, the old side with no bold.
      - Added: only when no old criterion checks the same thing (a new destination changes the sends one). Keeps the bold `write_ai_task_brief` gives it. Removed: `▢ ~~<old>~~`, with no bold.
    - **Follow-up:** only the draft report's "Attach <next-best> instead" button, always when this change added or switched the attachment and `add_ai_task_delivery` kept a pick of the other kind.

    ````
    ## ✅ Task updated

    Still a draft: click `Commit changes`, then `Publish` to apply.

    | | |
    |---|---|
    | 🗓️ Schedule | ~~Mondays 9:00 AM UTC~~ → Mondays **8:00 AM** UTC |

    ### Acceptance criteria

    ▢ ~~Covers revenue by category in the Monday–Sunday week~~ → Covers revenue and **share of the weekly total** by category in the Monday–Sunday week

    ▢ States **both weeks' dates** and that the data is complete

    ### Files

    ```artifact
    <artifact id of each changed file's last save>
    ```

    [Attach <next-best> instead](#opt)
    ````

    If saving keeps failing, reply "## ❌ Couldn't update the task", the reason in plain words, and what the user can do.
  ;;
}
